---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import ServiceCard from '../../components/ServiceCard.astro';
import CTABlock from '../../components/CTABlock.astro';

const related = [
  { title: 'Land Clearing', description: 'Removing brush, trees, and debris to open up usable land.', href: '/services/land-clearing' },
  { title: 'Brush Clearing', description: 'Cutting back overgrowth for defensible space or usable acreage.', href: '/services/brush-clearing' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Land Clearing Cost Per Acre in Oregon | D&D Land Works"
	description="Land clearing cost per acre in Oregon depends on vegetation density more than acreage. What drives the price, with real cost data. Free estimates."
>
	<Hero
		eyebrow="Cost Guide"
		headline="Land Clearing Cost Per Acre"
		subheadline="An acre of pasture grass and an acre of second-growth timber are not the same job, and they're not close to the same price."
		primaryCta={{ label: 'Call 541-401-8726', href: 'tel:5414018726' }}
		secondaryCta={{ label: 'Get an Estimate', href: '/contact' }}
	/>
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16">
		<h2 class="font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-3xl text-ink">
			Vegetation Density Sets the Price
		</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
			<a href="https://www.angi.com/articles/how-much-does-it-cost-clear-land.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand-blue underline hover:text-brand-blue-dark">Angi's 2026 cost data</a> puts
			land clearing nationally between $1,200 and $8,000 per acre, and the spread comes almost
			entirely from what's actually growing on the land. Light brush and grass run closer to $600
			to $1,300 an acre. Shrubs and small trees push that to $2,100 to $4,100. Heavy timber, the kind
			of second-growth Douglas fir common around Cottage Grove and Oakridge, runs $3,600 to $6,100
			or more. Some contractors price by the hour instead, typically $120 to $265.
		</p>
		<h2 class="mt-12 font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-3xl text-ink">
			What Changes the Number Beyond Vegetation
		</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
			Blackberry and scotch broom, the two most common overgrowth problems on Lane County acreage,
			clear faster than standing timber but layer thick enough after a few seasons to slow a brush
			hog down. Slope matters too. A flat parcel out toward Junction City clears quicker than a
			hillside lot near Oakridge, where equipment has to work more carefully around grade. What
			happens to the material afterward, whether it gets hauled off, chipped, or burned where
			permitted, adds its own cost on top of the clearing itself.
		</p>
		<ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-slate-700 list-disc list-inside">
			<li>Vegetation type: grass and brush clear faster than standing timber</li>
			<li>Density: overgrown blackberry can slow a job as much as small trees</li>
			<li>Terrain: slope and soil stability affect equipment access</li>
			<li>Debris handling: hauling, chipping, or burning each carry their own cost</li>
			<li>Acreage: larger parcels often price slightly lower per acre than small ones</li>
		</ul>
		<h2 class="mt-12 font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-3xl text-ink">
			Getting an Accurate Number
		</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
			A per-acre average is a starting point, not a quote. David walks the property, looks at what's
			actually growing on it, and prices the job based on that, not a spreadsheet formula. Licensed
			and bonded under CCB #261742, serving Eugene, Springfield, and the rest of <a href="/service-area" class="text-brand-blue underline hover:text-brand-blue-dark">Lane County</a>.
		</p>
	</section>
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pb-16">
		<h2 class="font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-2xl text-ink text-center">
			Related Services
		</h2>
		<div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
			{related.map((service) => <ServiceCard {...service} />)}
		</div>
	</section>
	<CTABlock
		headline="Get a Real Number for Your Property"
		subheadline="Free on-site estimate for land or lot clearing."
	/>
</BaseLayout>
